Check the SBR frame borders.

extractFrameInfo() trusted the frame grid: up to 8 envelopes (FIXFIX)
or 7 (VARVAR) for tables of MAX_ENVELOPES (5), a
bs_pointer past the envelopes (middleBorder, lA indexing before tE[]),
and relative borders that ran past the trailing one. Decreasing borders
made the envelope adjustment and the energy estimation address QMF slots
past their buffers, and write over the SBR frame data (heap overflows in
calc_sbr_envelope.cpp and decode_noise_floorlevels.cpp). The frame is
now rejected (ISO/IEC 14496-3, 4.6.18.3.3: borders do not decrease).

Regression input:
tools/aacdec-fuzz/regressions/t169-sbr-frame-borders.bin.

